# A store into a reference field `@: Model q` of a merge result admits the
# value to Model, as the same store through the declared Structure does: an
# Other of another shape (two ints, no size_t `value`) is refused -- the
# method's implicit throw `implements`, uncaught, stops R0. It was a plain
# unchecked store.
Model: (size_t: value 1U)
Other: (int: p 1; int: q 2)
Holder:
    @: Model q
end: Holder

fn: check () int
    h: merge: Holder
    o: merge: Other
    h\q: o
    return: 7
end: check

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
